{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If it happens.</b> This passage is juxtaposed here because it writes <b>on the road</b> in it — and 'on the road' is what it speaks of." "<b>A bird's nest.</b> In every place where צפור is stated, the verse speaks of a clean bird, but an unclean bird is not subject to shiluach (sending away). As Rabbi Yitzchak said: a clean bird is called עוף and is called צפור, but the unclean one is called only עוף." "<b>You shall not take the mother upon the young.</b> Because it is a way of cruelty and gluttony. And similarly, a kid in its mother's milk, and similarly, it and its son, and similarly, fourth-year planting." "<b>Upon the young.</b> With the young. Patterned after ״upon the field of the earth it is reckoned,״ ״upon the daily burnt-offering,״ ״upon the wood — burn.״"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {3 "The three scriptural parallels cited are fragmentary; the third (על פרשה ישרוף) appears to be a truncated quotation, possibly from Lev 6:5–6 or a similar passage about burning on the wood; translated hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:49.272533661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}